From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mio <mio@mio19.uk>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 21:37:12 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] Keep QML diagnostics in the launcher's logged categories

`QT_LOGGING_RULES` started with `*=false`, which also disables the default
category, so QML import and instantiation errors were never written to
launcher.log or the console. On a black-screen boot that left only
renderloop chatter, with no trace of why the launcher's scene was empty.
Re-enable default warnings and qt.qml.* so the failure is visible.
---
 examples/asteroid/asteroid-desktop.nix | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/examples/asteroid/asteroid-desktop.nix b/examples/asteroid/asteroid-desktop.nix
index c7a27ff7..6964ccad 100644
--- a/examples/asteroid/asteroid-desktop.nix
+++ b/examples/asteroid/asteroid-desktop.nix
@@ -651,7 +651,11 @@ in
         # These are runtime switches only; the upstream code path is unchanged.
         # Keep the graphics/EGL diagnostics, drop the QML import flood so the
         # actual failure stays at the end of launcher.log.
-        QT_LOGGING_RULES = "*=false;qt.qpa.*=true;qt.waylandcompositor.*=true;qt.scenegraph.*=true;qt.core.plugin.*=true";
+        # Keep default-category warnings and QML diagnostics on: `*=false`
+        # also silences qWarning(), which is where QML import/instantiation
+        # errors are reported, leaving nothing but renderloop chatter in the
+        # log when the launcher's scene comes up empty (black screen).
+        QT_LOGGING_RULES = "*=false;default.warning=true;qt.qml.*=true;qt.qpa.*=true;qt.waylandcompositor.*=true;qt.scenegraph.*=true;qt.core.plugin.*=true";
         QT_DEBUG_PLUGINS = "1";
         EGL_LOG_LEVEL = "debug";
         LIBGL_DEBUG = "verbose";
